@title Checkout Payment Flow
@subtitle In-app checkout design, version 2
@author Payments Engineering, Tidewater Grocers
@date 2026-09-22

## Payment sequence
diagram pay sequence title="Checkout payment (happy path)"
pay: app "Mobile App" user
pay: api "Checkout API" svc
pay: fraud "Fraud Service" svc
pay: gw "Payment Gateway" ext
pay: ledger "Ledger" db
pay: app -> api : POST /checkout with cart and card token
pay: api -> fraud : score order
pay: fraud --> api : risk score
pay: note api : risk score 80 or below continues
pay: api -> gw : authorize amount
pay: gw --> api : auth code
pay: api -> ledger : record pending charge
pay: ledger --> api : entry id
pay: api --> app : order confirmed

diagram stepup sequence title="Alternative: risk score above 80"
stepup: app "Mobile App" user
stepup: api "Checkout API" svc
stepup: fraud "Fraud Service" svc
stepup: gw "Payment Gateway" ext
stepup: app -> api : POST /checkout with cart and card token
stepup: api -> fraud : score order
stepup: fraud --> api : risk score
stepup: note api : score above 80, Payment Gateway not called
stepup: api --> app : step-up verification required

## Latency budget
data latency = Step,p95 budget (ms),Measured p95 (ms); Fraud scoring,120,96; Authorization,450,512; Ledger write,40,31; Total checkout,800,811
table latency
chart bar latency x=Step y=p95 budget (ms),Measured p95 (ms) unit=ms title="p95 budget vs measured"

## Open issues
!! Authorization is over budget by 62 ms because the gateway's us-east endpoint is called from us-west-2.

Next steps:
- Move to the gateway's regional endpoint.
- Add a 2 second timeout with one retry.
- Alert when total checkout p95 exceeds 800 ms.
